I don't think so. We already have polymorph traps in NH, where in one
stroke you can lose your armor and cloak and be transformed into a
grid bug (I speak from personal experience.) We have gnomes that pop
out of nowhere and zap us with wands of death. We have all sorts of
unexpected bad things. But nobody's quit playing the game yet because
of that.

I'm not talking about constant changes here, just that, maybe once
every few hundred turns, a single object of yours changes shape.
Perhaps some restrictions could be set (i.e. your weapon and armor
don't change). Or perhaps everything you carry in your main inventory
won't change; only items you drop or carry in a bag are in danger of
polymorphing.

The reason I proposed this idea is that I think it would help to
increase *creative* solutions to problems. Many players tend to rely
on a single solution (e.g. wand of death) to all their really serious
problems. By Gehennom you tend to have collected so much useful
equipment that you can just blast your way through the dungeon without
really thinking about it. But if you're fighting that MMF, and find
that your wand of death has suddenly transformed into a wand of light,
you're going to have to do some very fast thinking...

